      "final_message": "Good. All changes are applied correctly. Here's a summary of what was fixed:\n\n**Three changes across three files:**\n\n1. **`SessionTracker.ts`** \u2014 Added `startNewSession()` method that records the actual meeting start time by setting `sessionStartTime = Date.now()`. Previously, `sessionStartTime` was only set at construction (app launch) or during `reset()` (previous meeting end), so the duration calculation was always wrong.\n\n2. **`IntelligenceManager.ts`** \u2014 Added `startSession()` delegate that calls through to `session.startNewSession()`.\n\n3. **`main.ts`** \u2014 Two fixes:\n   - **Start**: Call `this.intelligenceManager.startSession()` in `startMeeting()` so the session start time is recorded when the meeting actually begins.\n   - **End**: Swapped the order in the teardown \u2014 `stopMeeting()` (which saves the placeholder to DB) now runs BEFORE `broadcastMeetingState()` (which tells the UI the meeting ended). Previously, the UI was told the meeting ended before it was saved, so the launcher would fetch meetings and not find the new one.",
